§. 21. Direct. 18. Live as in a constant course of obedience; and suppose you saw the Law of God
also written upon every thing you see. As when you look on any tempting beauty; suppose you saw this written on the forehead, [Thou shalt not lust: Whoremongers and Adulterers God will judge: They shall not enter into the Kingdom of God:] See upon the forbidden dish or cup the prohibition of God, [Thou shalt not eat, or drink this]: See upon money and riches this written, [Thou shalt not cove•
]: See upon the face of all the world, [Love not the world, nor the things that are in the world: If any man love the world, the Love of the Father is not in him.] Thus see the Will of God on all things.
